rota lap 6965, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears. Read foundations/20260826-021731_aether-the-row-that-hears.md whole. The lap's own purpose rhymes with the row's cardinal/fixed/dual triad: a witness this tree already built, proven both ways, stood as an honest silence on the roster -- no guard read it, no lap could cite it by name -- and this lap's whole work was making it sound. The Lindy fixed seat's own line landed hardest: a guard that cannot red guards nothing, a witness must be proven able to make a sound before its silence means anything -- which is exactly what shed_census_witness.rish already did inside one file, and exactly what the roster row now lets the rest of the fleet hear.
